{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Dnd6DCi16DRN2FAGVqGDt","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me compile the final report:\n\n## Summary: Experiment Configurations, Pilot Results, and Analysis Scripts\n\nI've thoroughly explored the project at `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1`. Here are the key findings organized by category:\n\n---\n\n## 1. EXPERIMENT CONFIGURATION FILES\n\n**Location**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/`\n\n### Main Configuration Files:\n- **`experiment_plan.yaml`** — Master experiment plan with 11 experiments (exp-001 through exp-011)\n  - Organized by priority: P0 (51 GPU-hours), P1 (12 GPU-hours), P2 (5 GPU-hours)\n  - Key P0 experiments: NER N=16 validation, CoNLL-2003, WNUT-17 cross-dataset generalization, RE diagnostic analysis, temperature sensitivity analysis\n  - Contains claims, datasets, GPU budgets, and dependencies\n\n- **`registry.yaml`** — Complete experiment registry tracking all completed/in-progress experiments\n  - Records: ft_001, ft_002, ft_002_v2, mvp_pilot_001-005, e1_component_wise_re_sj\n  - Each entry includes: status, metrics, timestamps, model configs, data paths, conclusions\n\n- **`dream_registry.yaml`** — Research simulation/dream planning\n  - Single dream session: dream_20260514T093336 (status: imagining, full review mode)\n  - Focuses on multi-dataset NER generalization and RE diagnostic findings\n\n- **`decisions.yaml`** — Decision log documenting 10 major decisions (D001-D010)\n  - Key decisions: MVP approach selection, metric thresholds (0.40 for PASS, 0.30 for MARGINAL), gate0/gate1 criteria, narrative strategy (A: NER-primary + RE diagnostic)\n\n- **`artifacts/manifest.yaml`** — Artifact inventory tracking all code modules and reports\n  - 17 artifacts: consistency.py, evaluation.py, sampling.py, data_utils.py, run_mvp_pilot.py, various reports\n\n---\n\n## 2. PILOT RESULTS (mvp_pilot_003, mvp_pilot_004, e1_component_wise)\n\n### MVP Pilot 003 Results\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/logs/workers/worker_eval_mvp_pilot_003_20260514T080934_result.json`\n\n**Key Metrics (N=8, T=1.0, 551 SciERC test instances)**:\n- **NER**: rho_sj = 0.3808 (p=1.07e-19), rho_fk = 0.3362; SJ beats FK (Δ=+0.0446); oracle headroom +15.6pp\n- **RE**: rho_sj = 0.2367 (p=1.85e-06), rho_fk = 0.2221; SJ beats FK (Δ=+0.0146); oracle headroom +21.7pp; 67.6% zero F1 samples\n- **Verdict**: FAIL (RE rho_sj < 0.40 threshold)\n- **Key fixes vs pilot_001**: max_tokens=1024 eliminated all parse failures (0 vs 164); NER/RE both slightly improved\n\n### MVP Pilot 004 Results  \n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/logs/workers/worker_eval_mvp_pilot_004_20260514T085219_result.json`\n\n**Key Metrics (N=8, T=1.0, ft_002_v2 improved model)**:\n- **NER**: rho_sj = 0.3825, rho_fk = 0.2590; SJ beats FK decisively (Δ=+0.1235); oracle headroom +10.9pp\n- **RE**: rho_sj = 0.2441, rho_fk = 0.2782; **SJ loses to FK on full set** (Δ=-0.0341); conditional rho_sj = 0.3161 (good); oracle headroom +16.7pp; 44.3% zero F1\n- **Verdict**: FAIL (RE rho_sj < 0.30)\n- **Findings**: Model quality improved (F1: NER 66.7%, RE 42.1%), but RE signal still weak. SJ's weakness on RE persists despite better base model.\n\n### E1: Component-wise RE Decomposition Analysis\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/logs/workers/worker_analysis_e1_component_wise_re_sj_20260514T091631_result.json`\n\n**Key Finding: Multiplicative Penalty Hypothesis REJECTED**\n\n| Component | Full ρ | Conditional ρ |\n|-----------|--------|---------------|\n| head_sj   | 0.210  | 0.270         |\n| tail_sj   | 0.201  | 0.259         |\n| type_match| 0.201  | 0.252         |\n| multiplicative | 0.244 | 0.316     |\n| additive  | 0.243  | 0.306         |\n| fleiss_kappa | 0.278 | 0.307       |\n\n**Conclusion**: \n- head_sj (0.210) is **far below NER rho (0.383)** — Δ = -0.173\n- Each component alone **underperforms the multiplicative combination**, indicating the composition is helping, not hurting\n- Additive aggregation is indistinguishable from multiplicative (difference = 0.001)\n- **Root cause**: Span-level soft Jaccard fundamentally lacks discriminative power for relation tasks; it's not a metric design issue but an inherent property of the task complexity\n\n---\n\n## 3. ANALYSIS SCRIPTS\n\n**Location**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/`\n\n### Core Analysis/Evaluation Modules:\n\n1. **`evaluation.py`** — Strict-match evaluation for NER/RE\n   - Functions: `entity_strict_match()`, `compute_ner_f1()`, `relation_strict_match()`, `compute_re_f1()`\n   - Provides: precision, recall, F1 metrics; per-instance F1 computation\n   - Used in: All MVP pilots for correlation analysis\n\n2. **`consistency.py`** — Consistency metric computations\n   - Implements: \n     - Fleiss' Kappa (surface-level agreement)\n     - Soft Jaccard with Hungarian matching (structural consistency)\n     - Oracle best-of-N selection\n   - Key function: `fleiss_kappa_surface()`, soft Jaccard computation with `linear_sum_assignment()`\n\n3. **`sampling.py`** — vLLM-based batch sampling\n   - VLLMSampler wrapper for Qwen3-8B\n   - XGrammar constrained JSON decoding\n   - Span realignment post-processing (fixes hallucinated character offsets)\n   - Output parsing and validation\n\n4. **`run_mvp_pilot.py`** — Main MVP experiment pipeline\n   - Orchestrates: data loading → sampling → consistency scoring → evaluation → correlation analysis\n   - Implements PASS/MARGINAL/FAIL verdict logic\n   - Reports: rho Spearman correlation, p-values, filtering statistics\n\n5. **`data_utils.py`** — Data processing for SciERC/ACE05\n   - Loads UIE JSON format\n   - JSONL I/O, dataset partitioning\n   - Handles char-offset conversions\n\n---\n\n## 4. METRIC DEFINITIONS & THRESHOLDS\n\n**Source**: `decisions.yaml`, `memory.md`, `registry.yaml`\n\n### Key Thresholds:\n\n| Threshold | Definition | Usage |\n|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| **0.40** | PASS threshold for rho_sj | Full set correlation must reach ≥0.40 to pass |\n| **0.30** | MARGINAL threshold | 0.30-0.40 range indicates partial signal; triggers T=0.7 protocol |\n| **< 0.30** | FAIL threshold | Confirms hypothesis failure; hard cutoff |\n| **> 30%** | Zero F1 rate trigger | If % samples with F1=0 exceeds 30%, activate T=0.7 experiment |\n| **NER gate0: 60.4%** | Fine-tuning quality gate | NER F1 must reach ≥73% for good model (ft_001 only reached 60.4%) |\n| **RE gate0: 40%** | RE quality gate | RE F1 must reach ≥40% (ft_001: 33.8%, ft_002_v2: 41.8%) |\n\n### Metrics Tracked:\n\n**Per-experiment metrics**:\n- `rho_sj` (full, conditional) — Spearman correlation of soft Jaccard vs per-instance F1\n- `rho_fk` (full, conditional) — Spearman correlation of Fleiss Kappa vs per-instance F1  \n- `p_sj`, `p_fk` — Statistical significance p-values\n- `sj_beats_fk` — Boolean: does soft Jaccard beat Fleiss Kappa\n- Sample F1 distribution: mean, std, % zero\n- Oracle headroom: best-of-N upper bound gain\n- Parse failures: stochastic and greedy counts\n\n**Filtering rules**:\n- Gold-empty instances: removed from analysis (28% of RE instances)\n- All-samples-F1=0 instances: counted separately for \"conditional\" rho\n- These filtering rules produce two rho values: \"full\" (before filtering) and \"conditional\" (after filtering)\n\n---\n\n## 5. ADDITIONAL CONFIGURATION & DOCUMENTATION\n\n- **`memory.md`** — Lessons learned, env setup instructions, E4 dataset survey (77 rows)\n- **`ROADMAP.md`** — Research stage dashboard, timeline (DDL: 2026-05-25), GPU budget\n- **`paper_framing.md`** — Narrative strategy (NER-primary claim + RE diagnostic analysis)\n- **`IDEA_BRIEF.md`** — High-level project scope and motivation\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Files by Path:\n\n| Category | Path | File |\n|----------|------|------|\n| **Experiment Config** | `projects/struct_self_consist_ie/` | `experiment_plan.yaml`, `registry.yaml`, `decisions.yaml` |\n| **Pilot Results (JSON)** | `logs/workers/` | `worker_eval_mvp_pilot_003_*_result.json`, `worker_eval_mvp_pilot_004_*_result.json`, `worker_analysis_e1_component_wise_re_sj_*_result.json` |\n| **Analysis Scripts** | `artifacts/` | `evaluation.py`, `consistency.py`, `sampling.py`, `run_mvp_pilot.py`, `data_utils.py` |\n| **Checkpoints** | `checkpoints/` | Status files for mvp_pilot_003, mvp_pilot_004, e1_component_wise_re_sj |\n| **Documentation** | `projects/struct_self_consist_ie/` | `memory.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `paper_framing.md` |\n\nAll results point to **NER showing strong structural self-consistency signal (rho ~0.38, SJ > FK by 12pp)** while **RE struggling due to compound error propagation** (rho ~0.24, well below the 0.40 threshold). The E1 analysis definitively rules out metric design as the cause—span-level soft Jaccard is fundamentally limited for relational tasks."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fc9b383-c417-43bc-b48d-b0a1903064d9","uuid":"b50f86e7-49ac-405d-84b4-d6c7e3873acc","timestamp":"2026-05-14T09:47:31.167Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the project at /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1, find any files related to experiment configurations, pilot results, or analysis scripts. Specifically look for:\n1. Any YAML/JSON config files for experiments\n2. Result files from completed pilots (mvp_pilot_003, mvp_pilot_004, e1_component_wise)\n3. Analysis scripts\n4. Any files containing metric definitions or thresholds\n\nSearch broadly - check directories like experiments/, results/, configs/, analysis/, scripts/, data/, etc. Report file paths and brief content summaries.","agentId":"ab32c6538eb152a3a","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perf